// Safe Mode boot set with bcdedit
//
// Fires when bcdedit changes the Safe Mode boot setting. Works whether or not the ASR Safe
// Mode rule is on. Setting it is the ransomware move. Clearing it right after a Safe Mode
// session is the cleanup.
//
// Runs:      Continuous (NRT)
// Severity:  High
// MITRE:     T1688
// Tables:    DeviceProcessEvents
// Custom details: AccountName
//
// Needs:
//   - Nothing beyond Defender for Endpoint.
//
// Triage (paste into Recommended actions):
//   - Check the command line, the account, and whether the device rebooted after.
//   - Escalate unless IT is fixing the device under a ticket.
//   - Close if it's ticketed repair work.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ingestion_time() > ago(1d)
| where FileName =~ "bcdedit.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "bcdedit.exe"
| where ProcessCommandLine has "safeboot"
| project Timestamp, ReportId, DeviceId, DeviceName, AccountName, FileName, ProcessCommandLine, InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessCommandLine
